From: desp <me@desp.lol>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:27:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/38] Shaders: the code table starts after the instructions
 (port of Marvisak/VIctory#2143)

The table code_dword reads was the program's code from the lowest offset
any load or descriptor names, and a load at a computed offset names
offset 0: the table was the whole program. Under vkd3d-proton that
constant array becomes a private one; NVIDIA's compiler keeps up to
16 KiB of such arrays in constant memory and copies a larger one into
every thread's local memory. On the RTX 5090 (GB202) the lighting
computes with 16-18 KiB tables fault (Xid 13, writes to unmapped
addresses); on other cards they make the driver reserve GBs of VRAM.

The program's constants follow its instructions, and a load at a
computed offset reads them, so the table now starts where the
instructions end, unless a load at a fixed offset reads below that.

Ported from Marvisak/VIctory#2143 (524e2834 and a68ae559, squashed;
only the test module's import list differs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

